        {
          "index_key": "qa.baseline.api.api-availability",
          "schema_version": 0,
          "attributes": {
            "assets": [],
            "draft_status": "published",
            "enable_logs_sample": null,
            "enable_samples": null,
            "escalation_message": "",
            "evaluation_delay": 300,
            "force_delete": null,
            "group_retention_duration": "",
            "groupby_simple_monitor": null,
            "id": "314372274",
            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · API Availability\n**WHAT:** API Availability: availability signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `qa` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `api-services` (api / service, tier3)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customers are affected now, or a mission-critical capability is unavailable.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** More than half of requests failing is an availability boundary, not a behavioral deviation. Sub-outage degradation is caught by the anomaly and burn-rate archetypes; this one exists to fire fast and unambiguously.\n\n**OWNER:** application-development · support best-effort · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/api-availability.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-api-health` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `api-services.qa.api-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-api-availability` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## API Availability — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/api-availability.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## API Availability — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/api-availability.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · API Availability\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-api-availability`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
            "monitor_threshold_windows": [],
            "monitor_thresholds": [
              {
                "critical": "0.5",
                "critical_recovery": "",
                "ok": "",
                "unknown": "",
                "warning": "0.2",
                "warning_recovery": ""
              }
            ],
            "name": "[P3][qa][api] API Availability (baseline)",
            "new_group_delay": 300,
            "new_host_delay": 300,
            "no_data_timeframe": 0,
            "notification_preset_name": "",
            "notify_audit": false,
            "notify_by": [],
            "notify_no_data": false,
            "on_missing_data": "",
            "priority": "3",
            "query": "sum(last_10m):sum:trace.http.request.hits{env:qa,alert_band:baseline,service_archetype:api,http.status_class:5xx} by {service}.as_count() / sum:trace.http.request.hits{env:qa,alert_band:baseline,service_archetype:api} by {service}.as_count() \u003e 0.5",
            "renotify_interval": 60,
            "renotify_occurrences": 3,
