            "include_tags": true,
            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Worker Stopped Processing\n**WHAT:** Worker Stopped Processing: availability signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `qa` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `worker-platform` (application / service, tier3)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customers are affected now, or a mission-critical capability is unavailable.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Zero work processed in 30 minutes is an absolute liveness boundary for a continuously-fed worker; there is no statistical interpretation of zero.\n\n**OWNER:** sre · support best-effort · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/worker-stalled.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-app-health` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `worker-platform.qa.worker-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-worker-throughput` · no error-budget impact (non-production)\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Worker Stopped Processing — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/worker-stalled.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Worker Stopped Processing — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/worker-stalled.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Worker Stopped Processing\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-worker-throughput`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
